      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\"Developers using the IDE expect that references to issues in comments and commit messages are automatically turned into clickable links. The current configuration uses a regular expression that separates the two supported formats (\\\"#123\\\" and \\\"GLUTEN-123\\\") into two distinct capture groups. Because the link template only references the first capture group, references that match the second alternative are not resolved, breaking navigation for the \\\"GLUTEN-\\\" prefix. The required behavior is that any occurrence of either \\\"#\\\" followed by digits or \\\"GLUTEN-\\\" followed by digits should be recognized, and the numeric part should be captured in a single group that the link template can use to construct the correct URL. Update the IDE configuration so that the regular expression combines the two alternatives into one pattern with a single capturing group, ensuring that both forms are handled uniformly. The change must preserve the existing link template that inserts the captured number into the GitHub issue URL, and it should not interfere with any other IDE settings or project functionality.\"\n",
          "id": "prt_edef6abcf001JwV2Htmh2otVNR",
          "sessionID": "ses_12109544affe53WW3GR9pl4UWd",
          "messageID": "msg_edef6abce001zhTUrmSr9uzjJW"
        }
      ]
