        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nI can see the issue. The regex `#(\\d+)|GLUTEN-(\\d+)` has two separate capturing groups. When `GLUTEN-123` matches, the number is captured in group 2, but the link template uses `$1` which only works for the `#123` format.\n\nThe fix is to use a non-capturing group for the alternatives and a single capturing group for the digits:\n\n",
          "time": {
            "start": 1781857252918,
            "end": 1781857252941
          },
          "id": "prt_edef7f636001fFnqEWgWJYTfUZ",
          "sessionID": "ses_12109544affe53WW3GR9pl4UWd",
          "messageID": "msg_edef7dbef001Agyi2Zr8M7pilz"
